1. PURPOSE
The PCE Validation Taxonomy provides a comprehensive classification system for all possible failures, violations, and risk categories that must be checked when performing Prompt Compliance Engineering (PCE).
It ensures uniformity, auditable tracking, and deterministic scoring across all implementations of PCS-001-compliant systems.

2. SCOPE
This taxonomy governs:
Regulatory compliance checks
Industry readiness validation
Risk modeling and probabilistic outcome assessment
Self-adversarial audit verification
It applies to all AI-generated outputs subjected to PCE validation.

3. TAXONOMY STRUCTURE
Validation items are organized into four main domains, corresponding to PCS-001:
Regulatory & Policy Compliance (R)
Industry & Operational Readiness (I)
Risk & Probabilistic Outcome Modeling (P)
Self-Adversarial Audit Failures (S)
Each domain has:
Category: High-level group
Subcategory: Specific type of violation
Severity: Critical / High / Medium / Low
Description: Explanation
Failure Rule: Deterministic check
Mitigation Guidance: Optional remediation steps (informative)

