8. SEVERITY LEVEL DEFINITIONS
Critical: Automatic fail, cannot be mitigated post-validation.
High: Fail unless mitigated or revised.
Medium: Fail or warn; may be conditional.
Low: Warn only; does not block approval but should be addressed.

9. TAXONOMY USAGE RULES
All outputs must be scored against every domain and subcategory.
Failure in any Critical item = output rejection.
High/Medium/Low items contribute to scoring metrics and probabilistic success.
Audit logs must reference the code and reason for each violation.
Taxonomy updates require a version increment and public log.

